## Edge cases
- ERE translation: callers pass POSIX patterns like `^[[:space:]]*## Recommendation` and `^[[:space:]]*(schema_version|\{"no_issues_found)`. Confirm Python `re` matches the same way `grep -E` did; convert `[[:space:]]` and similar classes. Pre-validation must reject only genuinely invalid patterns (rc&gt;1 equivalent), not no-match.
- `close_fds` interaction: the verb runs under callers that capture stdout; verify KVs still arrive on the captured pipe via the `quiet_init` fd-3 dup, with no stray output to the real terminal.
- Embedded-space and newline-in-path: keep the line-oriented paths-file invariant and the pre-write newline/CR guard.
- `cap_hit` must bypass the gate; salvage must never fire on `empty`.

## Failure modes
- Orphaned subprocesses: if teardown misses a descendant, codex/cursor/claude can survive cancel. The SIGTERM teardown must kill the group and sweep descendants; the behavioral test pins this.
- Stale references: any remaining literal `scripts/dispatch-with-waterfall.sh` in a tracked, non-`larch-logs` file fails `make lint-retired-scripts`. The sweep plus the lint gate is the backstop; also check `scripts/test-design-multi-round-integration.sh` and `skills/design/scripts/review-design-step3-loop.sh` for residual literals.
- Embedded-blob drift: a regenerated blob that still points at the deleted path breaks plan-review panel/voter dispatch at runtime (lint will not catch it, since it is gzipped). The new pytest must decode both assets and assert they call `agent dispatch-waterfall` and not `dispatch-with-waterfall.sh`.

## Testing strategy
- `python3 -m pytest -q python/test_agent_waterfall.py` covering every accept/reject path above, including the SIGTERM teardown and the no-grouped-reuse guard.
- `python3 -m pytest -q python/test_decompose.py python/test_review_pipeline.py python/test_review_aggregate.py python/test_plan_review.py python/test_plan_review_panel.py` to confirm caller cutover and regenerated blobs.
- Parity gate before deletion: run the retired `scripts/test-dispatch-with-waterfall.sh` once against the new verb (temporarily) to confirm equivalence, then delete.
- `bash scripts/test-dispatch-code-voters.sh` (all sections) after the stub update.
- `make lint` + `make py-lint` + `make py-test` + `make lint-retired-scripts` all green.

